    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm looking at a contract for a shipment of electronic components coming from South Korea to Germany. It says CIF. can you explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for delivering the goods onto the vessel in the port of origin in South Korea. This responsibility includes paying for the cost of the goods, insurance covering the shipment, and the freight costs to the named port of destination in Germany. Importantly, risk transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods are loaded onto the ship in South Korea.",
