    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so just to be clear, if something happens to the electronics while they're being loaded onto the ship, who is actually on the hook for the loss? and does the seller have to provide any specific documentation for the insurance part?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the risk transfers to you (the buyer) once the goods are on board the vessel, you would generally be responsible for any loss occurring during loading. Regarding insurance, the seller must purchase minimum required marine cargo insurance under CIF terms and provide you with the insurance policy or a certificate of insurance. This documentation proves that the required insurance coverage was obtained before the goods shipped.",
